  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Carahsoft Technology obligated $1.4B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Carahsoft Technology won 1,462 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $951K. Carahsoft Technology's obligations are down 23.1% year over year. Carahsoft Technology's obligations by fiscal year show a rise from $1.2B in FY21 to $1.8B in FY24 and FY25, then a decline to $1.4B in FY26. Carahsoft Technology's top buying agency in FY2026 to date is the Department of Defense with $666M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $231M and the Department of Homeland Security with $109M. Carahsoft Technology's largest markets are Software Publishers with $971M and Other Computer Related Services with $212M, with additional activity across Custom Computer Programming Services and Electronic Computer Manufacturing. This fiscal-year snapshot represents partial totals for the year to date and reflects contract obligations rather than total contract values for the listed tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Carahsoft Technology's biggest federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $666M from Carahsoft Technology in FY2026 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $231M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $109M. The Department of Agriculture, General Services Administration, and Social Security Administration follow with $97M, $65.6M, and $59.8M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and products drive Carahsoft Technology's federal obligations?",
        "body": "Software Publishers is the largest market for Carahsoft Technology with $971M in obligations. Other Computer Related Services is the second market with $212M, and Custom Computer Programming Services accounts for $64.4M. Carahsoft Technology also appears in Electronic Computer Manufacturing with $20.8M and smaller markets such as Computing Infrastructure Providers with $2.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
